--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFW C-layer 6: the low bits by digit pieces (uniform)*: On the low `D'` bits (strides `2^{ρ + K (D' - 1 - x)} S`, `B' 2^{K D'} S` records), the recursive
--   procedure `lowC` with loop registers `11 j`, `12 R`, `13 o`, `14 m^j`, `15 ES j` covers the bits
--   `o ≤ x < o + R` by pieces: while `R ≥ m^j` a level-`j` call on the bits `o … o + m^j - 1`,
--   then `j ↦ j - 1`.  `lowF g j R` sums `g` over the pieces (`lowF ES`: the scale, `lowF DWb`:
--   the width, `lowF 1`: the count).
